# Windows checkouts turn LF into CRLF, and a shell script with CRLF fails in a
# Linux container in the most confusing way available: the kernel reads the
# shebang as "/bin/sh\r", cannot find that interpreter, and the entrypoint
# reports "not found" — about the file, which plainly exists.
#
# Anything executed inside a container stays LF regardless of the platform.
*.sh            text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
Dockerfile.*    text eol=lf
entrypoint.sh   text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
